{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A world holds data: entities and their components, and resources. A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"system"}]},{"type":"text","text":" holds a rule: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"step that reads part of the world and changes part of it, such as “every entity with a velocity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moves” or “gravity pulls on everything that isn’t frozen.” A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"schedule"}]},{"type":"text","text":" lists the systems of one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frame or step and runs them on a world, each once per run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and event:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double, y: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double, dy: Double }","struct Health: Component { var current: Int }","struct Frozen: Component {}","","struct Score: Resource { var points: Int }","struct TimeStep: Resource { var seconds: Double }","struct Paused: Resource {}","","struct Damage: Event { var target: Entity, amount: Int }"]},{"text":"Declare a System","type":"heading","anchor":"Declare-a-System","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The simplest way to write a system is to mark a type with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@System","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro and give it a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method. The method’s parameters say what the system works on, and their types say how:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" writes components, a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" reads them, and a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads a resource. The following two systems pull everything that isn’t frozen downward, then move","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it by its velocity:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@System","struct Gravity {","    func run(_ falling: Update<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        falling { velocity, _ in velocity.dy -= 10 }","    }","}","","@System","struct Movement {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","            position.y += row.components.dy","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because the parameters’ types state what each system reads and writes, the macro writes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for you: "},{"code":"Gravity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"Movement","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads "},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A schedule uses the access to decide which systems can run at the same time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also conform a type to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"},{"text":" by hand and write its ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)"},{"text":" method, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"receives the whole world. See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"},{"text":" for when to do that.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Run Systems in a Schedule","type":"heading","anchor":"Run-Systems-in-a-Schedule","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule"},{"type":"text","text":" is built from a list of systems, written in a result builder. Running it runs each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system once. The following example drops a ball for one frame:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 90.0)\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems run in the order you write them, unless an ordering constraint says otherwise."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"after(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"before(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" require one system to run after or before another; "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names a group of systems so constraints can refer to all of them at once; and "},{"code":"runIf(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" skips"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a system when a condition doesn’t hold."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems whose accesses don’t conflict, because neither writes what the other reads or writes,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run at the same time, and the world ends as though they had run one after another (commands"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"apply when each wave finishes). Systems that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conflict run in order. When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, their order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rests only on how they happen to be written; "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()"},{"type":"text","text":" finds those pairs so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"test can keep a schedule free of them. To learn more, see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"title":"Systems","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"Systems","role":"collection"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"]},{"anchor":"System-Parameters","title":"System Parameters","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents"]},{"anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules","title":"Building and Running Schedules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"]},{"anchor":"Main-Actor-Systems","title":"Main-Actor Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"]},{"anchor":"Built-In-Systems","title":"Built-In Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges"]},{"anchor":"Profiling","title":"Profiling","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming"]}],"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventWriter":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventwriter","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventWriter"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventWriter"}],"role":"symbol","title":"EventWriter","abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that sends events of one type.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemSet":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemSet","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemSet","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A type that names a group of systems, so ordering constraints can refer to all of them at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once.","type":"text"}],"title":"SystemSet","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemset"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardChanges":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ForwardChanges"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ForwardChanges"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that yields each component of one type added or changed since it last ran to an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asynchronous stream, with its entity."}],"title":"ForwardChanges","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardchanges"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduleBuilder":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulebuilder","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduleBuilder"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduleBuilder"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A result builder that collects the systems written in a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","isActive":true},{"text":"’s closure.","type":"text"}],"title":"ScheduleBuilder","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemTiming":{"title":"SystemTiming","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemtiming","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemTiming"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The times one system of a schedule has taken to run."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemTiming"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/MainActorSystem":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/mainactorsystem","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MainActorSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MainActorSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that runs on the main actor, for work that touches main-actor state such as a user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interface."}],"title":"MainActorSystem","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DeclaringSystems":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/declaringsystems","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Declaring Systems","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write the rules of a simulation as systems, and let their parameters state what they read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write."}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"Systems","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A rule that reads and changes a world, run once each time its schedule runs."}],"title":"System","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Ambiguity":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Ambiguity"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Ambiguity"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Two systems of a schedule whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint orders, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the order they run in rests only on the order they were written in.","type":"text"}],"title":"Ambiguity","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/ambiguity"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/run(in:)":{"role":"symbol","required":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"run","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"title":"run(in:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs the system’s rule once on a world."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/run(in:)"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/ambiguities()":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV","text":"Ambiguity","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"ambiguities()","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns every pair of systems whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"orders."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguities()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemParameter":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemparameter","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"SystemParameter","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type a system’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method can take in place of the whole world, whose type states what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the system reads and writes."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SystemParameter","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemParameter","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/CyclicOrdering":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CyclicOrdering"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CyclicOrdering"}],"title":"CyclicOrdering","abstract":[{"text":"An error indicating that the ordering constraints of a schedule’s systems form a cycle, so no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order satisfies them all.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/cyclicordering"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventReader":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads the events of one type sent since the system last read them."}],"title":"EventReader","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventreader"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardEvents":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ForwardEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ForwardEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that yields each event of one type to an asynchronous stream, so code outside the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schedule can await the events."}],"title":"ForwardEvents","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardevents"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/drivingaworldfromanapp","title":"Driving a World from an App","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Hold a world in your app or game engine, feed it each frame’s input, and let the objects outside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it read results and take part in a step."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/access":{"role":"symbol","required":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","defaultImplementations":1,"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"access"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6AccessV","text":"Access"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The component, resource and event types the system reads and writes, or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" if it may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change anything.","type":"text"}],"title":"access","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/access"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile":{"title":"SystemProfile","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile","abstract":[{"text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceWriter":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcewriter","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ResourceWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ResourceWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that reads and writes a resource.","type":"text"}],"title":"ResourceWriter","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduledSystem":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/scheduledsystem","kind":"symbol","title":"ScheduledSystem","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduledSystem"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduledSystem"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system together with the ordering constraints, sets and conditions a schedule runs it with."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SchedulingSystems":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Order the systems of a schedule, run them only when a condition holds, and find out how a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule runs them.","type":"text"}],"title":"Scheduling Systems","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulingsystems"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Query":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Query","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A description of the entities to visit and the components to read from each."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/query"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Schedule","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/UpdateEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/updateevents","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UpdateEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A system that ends the current event update, dropping events old enough that every reader","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has had its chance to read them.","type":"text"}],"title":"UpdateEvents","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UpdateEvents","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Update":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/update","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Update","abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that changes a component of every entity that holds it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceReader":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceReader"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceReader"}],"title":"ResourceReader","abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that reads a resource.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcereader"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/RemovedComponents":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RemovedComponents"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RemovedComponents"}],"title":"RemovedComponents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that lists the entities that lost a component since the system last read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/removedcomponents"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System()":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system()","kind":"symbol","title":"System()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Makes a type a system whose access comes from the parameters of its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()"}}}